---
/** The Promises and votes overview: status, both councils' member cards and
 *  how it works. It is the home page; member pages live under
 *  /promises-and-votes/<id>/. */
import Avatar from "~/components/Avatar.astro";
import CityVotesNote from "~/components/CityVotesNote.astro";
import { MUNICIPALITIES, formatDate, type Municipality } from "~/lib/data";
import {
  TERM_START, STATUS, membersOf, votesBy, chamberReplies, VOTES,
} from "~/lib/votes";

const munis: Municipality[] = ["cnv", "dnv"];
const count = (m: Municipality) => VOTES.filter((v) => v.municipality === m).length;
---
  <div class="notice">
    <p>
      <strong>It's early in the term.</strong> Both councils were sworn in on
      {" "}{formatDate(TERM_START)}, so there are very few votes yet, and most of
      the first ones are appointments and routine business. This fills in as
      councils vote and I review each one.
    </p>
    <ul class="pv-status">
      {munis.map((m) => (
        <li>
          <strong>{MUNICIPALITIES[m]}:</strong>{" "}
          {count(m) === 1 ? "1 vote" : `${count(m)} votes`} shown
          {STATUS[m].awaiting_review > 0 && <>, {STATUS[m].awaiting_review} more waiting for my review</>}.
          {" "}Last checked {formatDate(STATUS[m].retrieved)}.
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>
  </div>

  {munis.map((m) => {
    const members = membersOf(m);
    return (
      <section class="race-section" id={m}>
        <div class="race-heading">
          <h2>{MUNICIPALITIES[m]} council</h2>
          <span class="seats">{members.length} members</span>
        </div>
        {m === "cnv" ? (
          <CityVotesNote />
        ) : (
          <p class="pv-source">
            District votes come from the District's own{" "}
            <a href={STATUS.dnv.source_page} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Council
            voting decisions</a>{" "}table, where the District records how each
            member voted. It is usually updated within about two days of a vote.
            {count("dnv") === 0 && STATUS.dnv.awaiting_review === 0 && (
              <>
                {" "}As of {formatDate(STATUS.dnv.retrieved)} it shows no votes by
                the new council yet. Its only entry since they took office is an
                orientation workshop where no motion was put.
              </>
            )}
          </p>
        )}
        <div class="grid grid-2" style="margin-top:14px">
          {members.map((c) => {
            const said = c.positions.length + chamberReplies(c).length;
            const voted = votesBy(c).length;
            return (
              <div class="card card-link">
                <div class="candidate-row">
                  <Avatar candidate={c} />
                  <div style="min-width:0">
                    <div class="candidate-name">
                      <a href={`/promises-and-votes/${c.id}/`}>{c.name}</a>
                    </div>
                    <div class="candidate-meta">
                      {c.office === "mayor" ? "Mayor" : "Councillor"}
                    </div>
                    <div class="candidate-meta" style="margin-top:6px">
                      {said === 1 ? "1 campaign quote" : `${said} campaign quotes`}
                      {" · "}
                      {voted === 1 ? "1 vote" : `${voted} votes`}
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
            );
          })}
        </div>
      </section>
    );
  })}

  <h2 id="how" style="margin-top:48px">How this works</h2>

  <h3>The campaign words</h3>
  <p>
    These are the same quotes as everywhere else on this site: what each
    person published before the election, copied word for word, with a link to
    where they said it. Where they answered the North Vancouver Chamber's
    questions on transportation and small business, those answers appear
    under those two issues too, labelled as replies. Nothing has been added
    since the election.
  </p>

  <h3>The votes</h3>
  <p>
    Only votes since {formatDate(TERM_START)}, when the new councils took
    office. The two municipalities publish their votes differently:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>District of North Vancouver:</strong> from the District's{" "}
      <a href={STATUS.dnv.source_page} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Council
      voting decisions</a>{" "}table, which records each member's vote. I show
      what it records, including "absent" and "N/A".
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>City of North Vancouver:</strong> read from the{" "}
      <a href={STATUS.cnv.source_page} target="_blank" rel="noopener">council
      minutes</a>, because the City publishes no vote table. The box above
      explains how, and what that can and can't tell you.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Purely procedural motions (approving the agenda, adopting minutes,
    adjourning) are left out. So are decisions made in closed session, unless
    council later releases them.
  </p>

  <h3>Matching a vote to an issue</h3>
  <p>
    A computer program drafts a suggestion for each vote: which of this site's
    issues it relates to, if any, and a one-sentence plain-language summary.
    I then read each vote against its official wording and decide. Nothing
    appears here until I have. Matching is a judgement, made by a person, and
    reasonable people could draw some lines differently. A vote listed under
    an issue means it relates to that issue. It doesn't mean it keeps or
    breaks anything anyone said.
  </p>
  <p>
    The one-line summaries are mine and are labelled "Our summary". The
    official wording is one click away on every vote, with links to the
    minutes and, where there is one, the video.
  </p>

  <h3>Updates and corrections</h3>
  <p>
    I check both councils' records about once a month. If something here is
    wrong, a vote, a match or a summary, email{" "}
    <a href="mailto:corrections@northvanvotes.ca">corrections@northvanvotes.ca</a>{" "}
    and I'll fix it. <a href="/methodology/">More on how this site is built.</a>
  </p>
